# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo when a release is archived.
# `doi` is the Zenodo concept DOI, which always resolves to the newest version.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use palmgeo in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "palmgeo"
abstract: >-
  palmgeo turns publicly available open geodata -- national, regional or
  municipal -- into a complete, verified static driver for the PALM model
  system: the input rasters and the configuration for PALM's palm_csd, for any
  number of nested domains. A staged, resumable pipeline that records the data
  sources, their licences and their age.
authors:
  - family-names: "Hauschopp"
    given-names: "Jens"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3856-0305"
    affiliation: "Institute of Meteorology and Climatology, Leibniz University Hannover"
version: "1.2.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23973676"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/meteohauschopp/palmgeo"
references:
  - type: thesis
    thesis-type: "Bachelor's thesis"
    title: "Generierung von dreidimensionalen Einzelbaumrepräsentationen basierend auf Fernerkundungsdaten"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Rentz"
        given-names: "Joana-Pauline"
    year: 2026
    institution:
      name: "Institute of Meteorology and Climatology, Leibniz University Hannover"
    languages:
      - de
    notes: "Single-tree detection, greenness criterion and canopy height model are ported from its scripts."
keywords:
  - PALM
  - static driver
  - palm_csd
  - large-eddy simulation
  - urban climate
  - open geodata
